      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c3cba9d458a806c4177f293",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Ever since they released the new standards I've been under the assumption they will be implementing a filter system eventually.  It'll be especially necessary if VRchat is going to continue to optimize in a way that the platform could be used on the new affordable lower-end Oculus and Vive systems that will probably dominate the VR market in the future.\n\nI'm 110% for a simple system that can filter avatars based on optimization ratings, or allow you to wholesale block an avatar based on its descriptor so no matter who wears it you'll never see it for more fine level of control for the end user.\n\nThe problem is, there needs to be a better alternative to the current grey robot.  Something that accurately represents a player's view / hands even when their avatar is blocked, as well as have an avatar that is less bulky than the current grey robots which can still be annoying and intrusive.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5c3ccef4fed97d40bd70f2d4",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5af5f97d56feb85f40086953",
        "alias": "Nutty Kite",
        "aliasID": "65c9517aed6eefce4c1ef62f",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/b3b7104e06ff3bc516e2bca67e03f982.png",
        "created": "2018-05-11T20:13:49.548Z",
        "name": "SHOKK",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-01-14T18:03:32.541Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 1,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c3cba9d458a806c4177f293",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Currently the system broad-strokes so heavily, this would pretty much block everyone. 1 Polygon over 70k or just a weird low poly avatar with a large bounding box, you'll be marked as very poor, put in the same category as someone who use 100s of Dynamic bone transforms. \nWhich is more intensive? Well it's obvious, the dynamic bones.\n\nThe system needs to be improved before any sort of automation or people will just not even use it cause it's basically the same problem as the Panic Mode we had before, where you shotgun everyone to grey avatars.\n\nI pretty much manually check most avatars to understand if they are even a performance detriment when they have that cause I understand how large of a net it casts.\nSo a big no from me till the current systems actually work, or else we're just gonna have so many half-baked systems that have terrible synergy.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5c3cdb4f77470b40916d60f3",
      "author": {
        "_id": "59b80cbbd1662e660835c7c5",
