      "_id": "5c4cdbc0ffcea436059cc821",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5b78b51f4c57643590fd8232",
        "alias": "Ready Coral",
        "aliasID": "65c28318ed6eefce4cbdb7a9",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/4647574ca2cb505da7f43e2e7159ea37.png",
        "created": "2018-08-19T00:09:03.248Z",
        "name": "LoneEevee",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2019-01-26T22:14:24.934Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 1,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5c3cba9d458a806c4177f293",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think an idea like this will fall flat, and fall hard too. The system is majorly flawed in many ways.\n\n1. Some aspects of your avatar that can be ranked on the performance scale don't cause that much of a performance hit at all, notably bound size and audio sources.\n\n2. The system cannot detect the performance hit of shaders, so if you only have one material but a maliciously unoptimized shader, your avatar will still be shown as Excellent but in reality have a terrible performance hit.\n\n3. The system has no weighting to it, basically meaning if one aspect is bad, the whole avatar is seen as terrible. If a system to autoblock \"unoptimized\" avatars were to be put in place, we'd at least need a more lenient system than what we have now, scaling the ranking of the avatar on a number of factors.\n\nBasically what I'm saying is your idea cannot be realized as of right now because of how things are laid out as of right now. Also, if your main goal is to have a \"personalized\" optimization solution, just use the Shield/Safety system. Literally nothing is stopping you from using it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
