  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-14T16:36:45.440Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would help VRChat to introduce a system where unoptimized avatars are automatically placed in a \"Hidden State\". The reason being is that as users fill a world with unoptimized avatars, the game can freeze, making it impossible to open up the menu and manually hide that users avatar. Of course, if a users avatar is unoptimized and automatically hidden, allow players to unhide such an avatar at their own risk. Show a warning to the player that their unoptimized avatar is not being shown by default, and that they must use a better optimized avatar to be shown to all players automatically. It really sucks to start a public instance of a world and have the room quickly flooded with unoptimized avatars until the game no longer runs. Considering even other instance privacy levels have the same problem, this quick-fix should suffice until unoptimized avatars cease to be a major issue.\n\nTLDR:\n- Hide unoptimized avatars from other players automatically. Players using optimized avatars are not affected.\n- Allow players to override this option (locally) at their own risk, with a quick warning dialog.\n- Display a warning/notification to the unoptimized player upon joining each world with a nagging dialog or simple on-screen text.\n\nThis would darn near force people to use well-optimized avatars in populated worlds, as well as protect those with moderate frame rates from dropping frames and ultimately freezing/crashing as unoptimized players join a world unannounced.\n\nNote: I completely understand that players don't like to be stigmatized for using unoptimized avatars, but game performance and stability is a must. As I suggested, this feature should be able to be disabled, lest all the unoptimized players throw a fit.",
